{{WeaponComparison|Aklex|header=n}}

==Acquisition==
A built Lex can be purchased from the [[Market]] for {{cc|50,000}}.

==Incarnon Genesis==
{{Transclude|Lex Incarnon Genesis#Acquisition}}

{{Transclude|Lex Incarnon Genesis#Incarnon Genesis}}

==Tips==
*Recommended to pair this with a close to mid-range primary weapon as its small magazine and longer reload times can be crippling at closer ranges. This weapon is also very useful while playing a support role for its long-range capability and common ammo type.
*This weapon is useful alongside automatic rifles or shotguns, as most of those weapons have poor long-range capabilities, and the {{M|Hawk Eye}} mod can increase zoom to effectively use it as a pocket sniper.
*This weapon can also be a high-risk-high-reward alternative to pair with a sniper rifle, since it can be used to finish off heavy enemies usually in a few hits, when you need to reload your rifle, or when you're being surrounded by lightly armored enemies.
*Using {{M|Steady Hands}} (which reduces the recoil of pistols) can be very beneficial to the Lex, as the high recoil between each shot could lead to you missing your target at times.
*{{WF|Mesa}}'s passive provides a much needed reload speed.

==Trivia==
*''[[wiktionary:lex#Latin|Lex]]'' is the Latin word for law, and short for Alexis or Alexander meaning "defender" and "defender from adversaries" respectively (from Greek: ἀλέξειν (''aléxein)'', meaning "defend").
**Lex also pronounced similar to ''เล็ก'' (Lĕk), a Thai word for "small", which is ironically referred to its tiny size.
**Lex shares its name with a mission node on [[Ceres]].
*The Lex has a surprisingly conventional appearance compared to most weapons in the game, drawing inspiration from real-world firearms. Its [[Lex Prime|Prime variant]] continues this trend, complete with a slide that is pulled back during reloading.
**The underbarrel attachment is a flashlight.
**The Lex appears to have two barrels, but the lower "barrel" is in fact a guide rod.
*The Lex and its [[Aklex|akimbo]] and [[Lex Prime|Prime]] variants share similar weapon sounds to the [https://darksector.fandom.com/wiki/Hammer_1895 Hammer 1895], a revolver featured in Dark Sector.

